text:
[2026-05-11 design-lock] All 5 design questions answered via interactive triage with Mark. Decisions:

**Q1 Scope:** Full coverage (Option B). Add CallerCtx to both JmapBackend (foundation) and every extension *Backend trait. Foundation jmap-server is in scope. Ripples to all 7 extension-server crates.

**Q2 Trait shape:** Associated type (Shape A), mirroring the existing type Error precedent.

```rust
pub trait JmapBackend: Send + Sync + 'static {
    type Error: std::error::Error + Send + Sync + 'static;
    type CallerCtx: Clone + Send + 'static;
    // ...
}
```

Declared on JmapBackend, inherited by all extension backend traits.

**Q3 Dispatcher relationship:** Single generic parameter on register fns; Dispatcher's C is named indirectly via B::CallerCtx.

```rust
pub fn register_mail_handlers<B>(
    dispatcher: &mut Dispatcher<B::CallerCtx>,
    backend: Arc<B>,
)
where
    B: MailBackend + 'static,
```

Multi-backend dispatchers (mail + chat + calendars on one dispatcher) work naturally: all registered backends must agree on CallerCtx at compile time, mismatch surfaced at the register_*_handlers call site.

**Q4 Read-side handlers:** Yes. Foundation handle_get / handle_changes / handle_query / handle_query_changes in crate-jmap-server/src/handlers.rs AND every per-domain wrapper in extension crates (handle_email_get, handle_mailbox_get, etc.) grow a caller parameter.

- 4a Name: `caller` (matches existing Dispatcher → JmapHandler → ClosureHandler chain)
- 4b Position: first after &self/&backend, before account_id/args
- 4c Mode: by reference (caller: &Self::CallerCtx)

Universal shape: `&self`/`&backend`, caller, account_id (or args), ...method-specific...

**Q5 Backwards-compat path:** Path A: hard break, single coordinated 0.2.0.

Rationale: Path B (associated-type-default) requires unstable `feature(associated_type_defaults)`, forcing jmap-server to nightly — hard no. Path C (parallel trait coexistence) doubles trait surface forever across 7 siblings and violates the cookie-cutter rule.

- 5a Document `type CallerCtx = ();` as canonical "no auth" idiom in JmapBackend rustdoc + update README boilerplate that currently says "deferred to a future version" (mail line 255, contacts line 201, sharing line 183, plus analogous in chat/calendars/tasks/filenode if present).
- 5b Every MemoryBackend reference impl across all 7 extension-server crates gets `type CallerCtx = ();` and `_caller: &()` on every method. Mechanical migration.
- 5c Single mega-PR touching jmap-server + all 7 extension-server crates atomically. Cookie-cutter rule prefers atomic propagation; intermediate broken-state is not a concern for workspace-internal path-deps.

**Macro shape inside register_mail_handlers** (cookie-cutter template for all 7 siblings):

```rust
macro_rules! reg {
    ($method:expr, $backend:expr, |$b:ident, $ci:ident, $a:ident, $ctx:ident| $body:expr) => {{
        let backend_arc: Arc<B> = Arc::clone(&$backend);
        let h: Arc<dyn JmapHandler<B::CallerCtx>> = Arc::new(ClosureHandler {
            backend: backend_arc,
            call_fn: Box::new(
                move |$b: Arc<B>, $ci: String, $a: serde_json::Value, $ctx: B::CallerCtx| {
                    Box::pin(async move { $body }) as HandlerFuture
                },
            ),
        });
        dispatcher.register($method, h);
    }};
}

reg!("Email/get", backend, |b, _ci, a, ctx| {
    handle_email_get(&*b, &ctx, a).await
});
```

**Implementation scope** (single mega-PR):

| Crate | Change |
|---|---|
| jmap-server | JmapBackend associated-type + method signatures + handle_get/changes/query/query_changes |
| jmap-mail-server (canonical) | MailBackend + all handle_* wrappers + register_mail_handlers/_mdn_/_sieve_ macros |
| jmap-chat-server | ChatBackend + handlers + register_chat_handlers (propagation) |
| jmap-calendars-server | CalendarsBackend + handlers + macro (propagation) |
| jmap-contacts-server | ContactsBackend + handlers + macro (.1.2 existing) |
| jmap-tasks-server | TasksBackend + handlers + macro (propagation) |
| jmap-filenode-server | FileNodeBackend + handlers + macro (propagation) |
| jmap-sharing-server | SharingBackend + handlers + macro (.1.3 existing) |

Plus 7 README boilerplate updates dropping "deferred to a future version".
Plus every MemoryBackend reference impl updated to `type CallerCtx = ();`.

**Unblocks:** .1.2 (contacts), .1.3 (sharing) — both were gated on this canonical's design being settled.

**Follow-up beads needed before mega-PR can land:** chat/calendars/tasks/filenode propagation beads + foundation update bead (currently missing from .1's children — epic title says "4 server crates" but new scope is 7 extension + 1 foundation = 8 sites).
